WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:08.975 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: On March 26, 2018
 a passenger train leaves
 Pyongyang, North Korea.</i>

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> 21 bullet proof cars
 painted an olive drab lumber
 across the countryside,</i>

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.622
<i> then over the Chinese border.</i>

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:27.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Rumors begin throughout
 the international community.</i>

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:32.197 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> This is the official train
 of the North Korea leadership.</i>

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Also used by
 Kim Il-Sung and Kim Jong-Il,</i>

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:40.573
<i> the grandfather and father of
 current leader, Kim Jong-Un.</i>

00:00:42.841 --> 00:00:47.147 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> No one outside of
 the notoriously secretive
 nation knows who is aboard.</i>

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:54.087
<i> Some speculate it is Kim
 Yo-Jong, Un's younger sister
 and most trusted advisor.</i>

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:01.661 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> It is not until the
 train reaches its final
 destination, Beijing,</i>

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:06.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> that it's revealed
 Kim Jong-Un, the
 34-year-old dictator himself,</i>

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:10.169
<i> is the passenger.</i>

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:12.472 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> In the months
 preceding this meeting...</i>

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.407
<i> What follows in Beijing...</i>

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.643
<i> And in the months to come...</i>

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:19.312
<i> Are the preliminary steps
 to what may be the most</i>

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:23.249 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> important diplomatic
 event of our young century.</i>

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:28.587 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> A path to peace on the
 Korean peninsula and a way
 to bring the North Koreans</i>

00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:32.425
<i> into the international fold
 after 70 years of isolation.</i>

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:40.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> But the path to peace will be
 one of twists and turns as
 allies and the US</i>

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:45.105
<i> jockey for position to
 protect their interests
 and maintain security.</i>

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:51.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> By the time President
 Donald Trump and Chairman
 Kim Jong-Un meet face to face</i>

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:57.083 align:start position:0%
<i>in Singapore, it is
still unclear what each party
wants or will be willing to do.</i>

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:02.789
<i> This is the Great Game.</i>

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:16.969
♪ ♪

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> North Korea
 remains an enigma.</i>

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:24.110 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Good Morning, how are you,
Mr. Vice President?

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.379
Very nice to see you.

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> NARRATOR: And only
 those who have sat
 across the table with</i>

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.084
<i> North Korean negotiators
 understand the challenges.</i>

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:38.124 line:0%
RICHARDSON: I do believe
that they're very tough,
they're very well prepared.

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:42.294 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
They read everything,
especially media.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
What makes them so tough,
it's not just their culture,

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.268 align:start size:84% position:16%
but the fact that
they've been isolated.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:50.836
They've been sanctioned.

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:55.008
They hardly any of
them, the citizens,
leave North Korea.

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.545
They have television that's
programmed every evening,

00:02:59.645 --> 00:03:02.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
for three hours
the government tells you
what you're going to see.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:05.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
And inevitably,
they hate the United States.

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:12.792 line:0%
HILL: At the end of the day,
diplomacy is really trying

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:16.062 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
to get the other
side to do something they
don't really want to do.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:22.568 align:start size:91% position:9%
in dealing with another
country, make it clear that
you make the hard choices

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:26.305
today and I'm not promising
you the end of hard choices,

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:30.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm promising you
that in the future you won't
have to make them alone.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.946 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
ALBRIGHT: Mostly, I
don't see it as a gift.

00:03:34.713 --> 00:03:38.251 line:0%
You usually use diplomacy
more with your adversaries
than with your friends.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:44.457 align:start position:0%
And so it is this matter
of being prepared and
putting yourself into the other

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
country's shoes and figuring
out what you do in order
to solve the problem,

00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:54.700
and it's not a gift.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.004 align:start size:88% position:13%
It is how you talk to
those you disagree with.

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:09.849 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The Democratic
 People's Republic of Korea,
 DPRK,</i>

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.585
<i> is anything but democratic.</i>

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:17.456
<i> From the ashes
 of World War II,</i>

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:20.960
<i> loomed the first post-war
 spread of Soviet communism.</i>

00:04:25.063 --> 00:04:29.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> In August 1945, the Korean
 peninsula and her people were</i>

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:33.005
<i> effectively divided
 at the 38th parallel.</i>

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:35.975
<i> An arbitrary divide.</i>

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:40.580 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Using a National Geographic
 map, the future US
 Secretary of state,</i>

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:45.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Dean Rusk
 and fellow army staffer
 Col. Charles "Tic" Bonesteel</i>

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:50.789
<i> knew the decision of the 38th
 parallel made no economic or</i>

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:55.962
<i> geographic sense, but
 with the cold war about
 to cast a long shadow,</i>

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:03.136 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> the United States wanted Seoul
 and the democratic leaning
 south, under their alliance.</i>

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:15.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Kim Il-Sung, the young
 charismatic rebel famous for
 his insurrection against the</i>

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:19.051
<i> brutal decades old
 Japanese occupation,</i>

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> vied for power and
 shaped this new republic in</i>

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:28.461 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> the Stalinist fashion
 adopting a totalitarian
 reign of terror.</i>

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:37.470
<i> Kim solidified his place in
 the soviet backed north, then
 sought to unify the peninsula</i>

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> by invading the south
 and starting the Korean
 conflict on June 25th, 1950.</i>

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:48.580
<i> Reporter (over TV): In an
 era of renewed optimism.</i>

00:05:48.680 --> 00:05:52.885 align:start position:0%
<i>NARRATOR: Three years
later a cease-fire was reached.</i>

00:05:54.119 --> 00:05:57.523 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> North Korea, a
 nation established by warfare,</i>

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:01.627 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> will be perpetuated
 by self-imposed
 isolation, bloodshed,</i>

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.464
<i> and humanitarian horrors.</i>

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
TERRY: It's the most
unique country in the world.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:14.907 align:start position:0%
What other country
in the world is Confucian,
communist, hereditary, dynasty,

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:19.011 align:start size:78% position:22%
there's no
country like this.

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:22.582 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
While it also commits
human rights violations.

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.316 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
United Nations Commission
of Inquiries said,

00:06:24.416 --> 00:06:27.920 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
"there's no other parallel
in contemporary history,
except Nazi, Germany"

00:06:28.153 --> 00:06:30.189
and this is North Korea.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:33.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think there is
another country that is more
isolated than North Korea,

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:39.131
so truly a unique place.

00:06:40.132 --> 00:06:43.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: And they have
 been challenging American
 policy, for nearly 70 years.</i>

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:49.308 align:start size:84% position:16%
HILL: I think any
political question has
to start with a map.

00:06:50.108 --> 00:06:54.413 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
And if you look at a
map of Northeast Asia,
it's a pretty compact area.

00:06:54.513 --> 00:06:57.282 align:start size:97% position:3%
You're seeing Russian
far east interest right there.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.485 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
You're seeing
Japan right there.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:02.788
China, enormous interest
right there, South Korea.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:04.891 align:start size:78% position:22%
And then, in
the middle of this,

00:07:04.991 --> 00:07:08.060
you have this funny little
thing called North Korea.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.964
How does it affect
the countries around
it and I would say,

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.466
it affects them all big time.

00:07:14.733 --> 00:07:17.336 align:start size:84% position:16%
TERRY: North Korea
has figured out how to
work the United States.

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:22.241 align:start size:97% position:3%
There is usually a provocation
of some sort, whether it is
a missile test or a nuke test.

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.845
Then there is international
condemnation that follows,

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then they sort of up
the ante, like a poker game.

00:07:28.881 --> 00:07:30.349
"Oh yeah? Here's more!"

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:33.051 align:start size:78% position:22%
Then, sort of a
collective "Oh no!"

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:37.189 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then they
step back and say, "OK.
Here is what we can do."

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:40.393
They have some sort of charm
offensive, peace offensive.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:44.496
Then we meet with them,
we negotiate, we give
them aids, some rewards,

00:07:44.596 --> 00:07:47.833
some time passes, then
back to provocation.

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.537 align:start size:78% position:22%
It's a provoke
and get paid cycle.

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:57.409
<i> NARRATOR: For generations,
 the North Korean
 people have been controlled</i>

00:07:57.509 --> 00:08:02.615 align:start position:0%
<i>by a police state that has
perfected propaganda to an art.</i>

00:08:03.816 --> 00:08:06.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Their belief in
 the Kim family dynasty,</i>

00:08:06.452 --> 00:08:09.055
<i> is absolute devotion.</i>

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:14.894
<i> Information is tightly
 controlled by the Korean
 central news agency,</i>

00:08:15.728 --> 00:08:18.964
<i> the KCNA, established in 1946.</i>

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:23.001 align:start size:84% position:16%
KRISTOF: There've
obviously been many
other deeply repressive

00:08:23.101 --> 00:08:25.837 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
Communist dictators,
Stalin, Mao.

00:08:25.937 --> 00:08:29.007 line:0%
They didn't have
the technology that
the Kim family had.

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:33.412 align:start size:97% position:3%
They didn't have the degree
of social control, so they
didn't have speakers on every,

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:36.481 align:start size:91% position:9%
in every village, speakers
in the wall of every
home to control people.

00:08:36.581 --> 00:08:38.784 align:start size:88% position:13%
They didn't have
television in every home.

00:08:38.884 --> 00:08:44.056 align:start size:97% position:3%
They didn't even have
these portraits of the leaders

00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:47.660
it's kind of a religious cult.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.195
RICHARDSON: It's the deity,

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:53.032
it's the leaders, the
grandfather, the father,
and now Kim Jong-Un,

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:57.436 align:start size:91% position:9%
that are not just
political figures, they're
god like religious figures.

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:02.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what they say determines
how North Koreans act.

00:09:03.842 --> 00:09:07.112
GAUSE: Kim Jong-Un only had a
very short amount of time to

00:09:07.212 --> 00:09:10.082 line:0%
build his legitimacy
within the regime.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:14.587 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Kim Jong-Il by comparison
had 30 years to create
his legitimacy.

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:20.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kim Jong-Un had none of this,
but a lot of things, very
interesting things began to

00:09:20.725 --> 00:09:23.395 align:start size:84% position:16%
happen when Kim Jong-Un
came to power.

00:09:23.495 --> 00:09:26.498 align:start size:81% position:19%
The first thing
that happened is they
had the missile test,

00:09:26.598 --> 00:09:28.267
which was a failure.

00:09:28.601 --> 00:09:29.801
But what does North Korea do?

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:32.304 align:start size:84% position:16%
They admit it was a
failure, unprecedented.

00:09:32.804 --> 00:09:34.372
Why did they do that?

00:09:34.473 --> 00:09:38.077 align:start size:88% position:13%
It gave people pause
to think that maybe this
was something different.

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:43.349
Kim Jong-Un laid down the
Rosetta Stone of where he
wanted to take this regime.

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:48.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
People would no longer
have to tighten their belts,

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:51.023 align:start size:88% position:13%
this was an important
statement by Kim Jong-Un.

00:09:51.123 --> 00:09:56.262 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was no mention
whatsoever of the nuclear
program in that speech because

00:09:57.229 --> 00:10:00.465 align:start size:91% position:9%
that's not where Kim
Jong-Un wanted his legacy.

00:10:00.565 --> 00:10:03.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was Kim Jong-Il's legacy
was the nuclear program.

00:10:04.236 --> 00:10:07.806 align:start size:84% position:16%
His legacy was to
create the strong
and prosperous nation.

00:10:08.206 --> 00:10:12.778 align:start size:91% position:9%
HILL: He then created
a kind of chaotic situation
within the worker's party,

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:18.450
the North Korean Workers'
Party and actually had
his uncle Jang Song-Thaek

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:22.254 align:start position:0%
perp-walked out of a party
meeting and killed the next day.

00:10:23.255 --> 00:10:28.794 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, Kim Jong-Un began a series
of executions of senior
North Korean figures

00:10:30.496 --> 00:10:36.202
such that it was hard to find
a common denominator of why
these people had been executed.

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:41.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
But certainly, one can
speculate that he didn't feel

00:10:41.974 --> 00:10:44.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
they were sufficiently
loyal to him.

00:10:45.911 --> 00:10:50.649
<i> NARRATOR: He purges over
 400 senior military and
 ministry leaders publicly.</i>

00:10:52.084 --> 00:10:56.589 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And allegedly has his
 older half-brother murdered
 in a Malaysian airport,</i>

00:10:57.656 --> 00:11:00.960 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> poisoned by
 unwitting assassins.</i>

00:11:03.662 --> 00:11:08.934
<i> But he needs something else
 to secure the Kim dynasty,
 nuclear weapons that could</i>

00:11:10.035 --> 00:11:13.839 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> pose a real and present
 danger to America
 and her Asian allies.</i>

00:11:16.274 --> 00:11:18.977
GAUSE: This would be
the launching of the
the Kim Jong-Un era.

00:11:19.077 --> 00:11:21.446
He had to show legitimacy.

00:11:21.546 --> 00:11:24.950
And if he couldn't
show legitimacy on
the economic realm,

00:11:25.051 --> 00:11:27.852
he had to show legitimacy
in the security realm.

00:11:28.353 --> 00:11:33.292
And so he began to move very
quickly towards developing
the nuclear program so that he

00:11:33.392 --> 00:11:35.193
would have something
to hang his hat on.

00:11:35.293 --> 00:11:37.863
So, it will give him a much
stronger position in which

00:11:37.963 --> 00:11:40.266
to negotiate with
the United States.

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:45.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: Kim Jong-Il
 moved the nuclear program
 forward in spite of</i>

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:50.643 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> international
 outcry and on again
 off again treaties.</i>

00:11:53.612 --> 00:11:57.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Now it is his son
 who may finish the job,</i>

00:11:57.917 --> 00:12:00.452
<i> having a strong hand to
 negotiate a way for his</i>

00:12:00.552 --> 00:12:04.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> impoverished nation
 to have an economic revival.</i>

00:12:06.759 --> 00:12:09.795 align:start size:97% position:3%
ALBRIGHT: I think that he
does have a good hand to play.

00:12:10.028 --> 00:12:15.701
I mean, he has in fact, from
his perspective, developed a
nuclear potential and missiles

00:12:17.402 --> 00:12:20.205
to do the delivery on it,
and he's managed to scare

00:12:20.305 --> 00:12:23.442 align:start size:81% position:19%
the whole region
into doing something.

00:12:34.319 --> 00:12:38.623 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: Through 2016
 to mid-September, 2017,
 Kim Jong-Un</i>

00:12:38.723 --> 00:12:42.695 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> conducts three nuclear tests,
 including a hydrogen bomb,</i>

00:12:43.629 --> 00:12:46.665 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> and 30 short and long-range
 missile launches;</i>

00:12:47.132 --> 00:12:50.536 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> including Intercontinental
 Ballistic Missiles.</i>

00:12:51.937 --> 00:12:54.173 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Kim claims that
 they have nuclear warheads</i>

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:57.676
<i> small enough to
 fit on each ICBM.</i>

00:13:01.647 --> 00:13:03.982
PRESIDENT TRUMP: In
70 years, in times
of war and peace...

00:13:04.082 --> 00:13:06.918 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: In September 2017
 president Donald Trump</i>

00:13:07.018 --> 00:13:09.287 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> addresses the
 UN General Assembly.</i>

00:13:09.955 --> 00:13:13.058 align:start size:84% position:16%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: No one
has shown more contempt
for other nations,

00:13:13.926 --> 00:13:19.398 align:start size:97% position:3%
and for the well-being of
their people than the depraved
regime in North Korea.

00:13:20.999 --> 00:13:24.436 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> NARRATOR: He delivers
 a fiery speech
 attacking Kim Jong-Un</i>

00:13:24.536 --> 00:13:27.139 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> and threatening the
 destruction of his country.</i>

00:13:28.006 --> 00:13:33.411 align:start size:97% position:3%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: Rocket man
is on a suicide mission for
himself, and for his regime...

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:39.517
<i> NARRATOR: Trump's rhetoric
 feeds directly into the
 north's propaganda machine,</i>

00:13:39.751 --> 00:13:42.854
<i> that America wants to
 annihilate North Korea.</i>

00:13:44.122 --> 00:13:47.058
TERRY: I think that was
definitely off script, I
can't impossibly imagine

00:13:47.859 --> 00:13:51.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
the administration
officials like Mattis
or Secretary Tillerson,

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
advocating totally
destroying North Korea,

00:13:55.467 --> 00:13:57.269 align:start size:81% position:19%
I just can't
possibly fathom that,

00:13:57.369 --> 00:13:59.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
so I think that was
President Trump speaking.

00:14:00.805 --> 00:14:04.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
KRISTOF: I think North
Korean officials have played
a weak hand just brilliantly.

00:14:05.977 --> 00:14:10.015 line:0%
While I think the US approach
has to some degree backfired.

00:14:10.582 --> 00:14:14.620 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Essentially the US was trying
to intimidate North Korea

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:18.490
with some of this rhetoric
about fire and fury,
about complete destruction.

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:23.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think what we actually
accomplished was that we
terrified South Korea into

00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:25.497 align:start size:81% position:19%
engaging in diplomacy
with North Korea.

00:14:26.698 --> 00:14:32.037 line:0%
ALBRIGHT: I think that it's
very hard to really assess
what effect President Trump's

00:14:32.938 --> 00:14:35.908
language had on Kim Jong-Un.

00:14:36.008 --> 00:14:38.910
I don't know whether it
scared the Japanese, too.

00:14:40.345 --> 00:14:43.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The United Nations
 Security Council votes
 for maximum pressure through</i>

00:14:44.016 --> 00:14:46.518
<i> economic sanctions
 against the north.</i>

00:14:46.852 --> 00:14:49.621 align:start size:97% position:3%
HALEY: We have kicked the
can down the road long enough.

00:14:49.721 --> 00:14:51.890
There is no more road left.

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:55.494
<i> NARRATOR: A war of words
 between Pyongyang and
 President Trump begins.</i>

00:14:55.794 --> 00:15:00.099 align:start size:97% position:3%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: North Korea
bess not make any more threats
to the United States.

00:15:01.834 --> 00:15:05.070 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: Kim
 refers to Trump as a
 "mentally deranged dotard."</i>

00:15:07.238 --> 00:15:10.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Trump insists his red
 button is bigger than Kim's.</i>

00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:19.784
<i> Still the DPRK tests another
 ICBM, this one experts agree,</i>

00:15:20.919 --> 00:15:24.556 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> has a range that could hit
 the continental United States.</i>

00:15:27.492 --> 00:15:29.894
<i> The US Talked openly
 about a "bloody nose"</i>

00:15:29.994 --> 00:15:32.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> military strike that would
 cripple nuclear testing sites.</i>

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:37.770 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Only a handful of
 experts believed this
 was a viable solution.</i>

00:15:41.473 --> 00:15:44.476 align:start size:91% position:9%
KRISTOF: Diplomacy is a
hugely inefficient toolbox.

00:15:44.576 --> 00:15:46.311
It doesn't work very well.

00:15:46.411 --> 00:15:49.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in cases like
North Korea, it's all we
have to resolve this crisis.

00:15:51.449 --> 00:15:54.753 align:start size:81% position:19%
Ever since 1969,
when North Korea shot
down a US aircraft

00:15:54.853 --> 00:15:57.689
and killed a bunch of Americans,

00:15:57.789 --> 00:16:01.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
the US has looked
for ways to shape
North Korean behavior.

00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:05.597 align:start size:91% position:9%
So repeatedly you have
very smart officials who,
when they're out of power,

00:16:05.697 --> 00:16:08.834
they talk about
military options.

00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:15.006
And then once in power, and
they look at the predictions
of perhaps a million-people

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:20.980 align:start size:91% position:9%
dying on the very first day
of a war with North Korea,
then they think well,

00:16:22.213 --> 00:16:24.382 align:start size:84% position:16%
okay maybe this
isn't the best option.

00:16:24.482 --> 00:16:26.084
And they look at what's left.

00:16:26.184 --> 00:16:28.987
And what's left is diplomacy.

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:31.857
<i> NARRATOR: Adding to
 the growing anxiety
 on the peninsula,</i>

00:16:31.957 --> 00:16:35.126
<i> south Korea was preparing
 the 2018 Olympic games.</i>

00:16:35.994 --> 00:16:40.566
<i> And there was precedent
 to feel insecure; thirty
 years earlier in 1988,</i>

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:45.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> South Korea's first
 Olympics were being planned.</i>

00:16:45.604 --> 00:16:49.541
<i> The supreme leader,
 Kim Il-Sung set out
 to create a chaotic</i>

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:52.644 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> atmosphere to keep
 people away from the games.</i>

00:16:53.611 --> 00:16:55.347
<i> JENNINGS (over TV):
 Investigators now
 believe that a bomb,</i>

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:58.483
<i> possibly planted by
 2 passengers may have
 caused Sunday's crash</i>

00:16:58.583 --> 00:17:00.886
<i> of a Korean Airliner.</i>

00:17:01.320 --> 00:17:05.123 align:start size:88% position:13%
TERRY: They downed a
civilian airliner, killed
115 people on board,

00:17:05.524 --> 00:17:07.726
it was a major terror attack.

00:17:07.826 --> 00:17:10.128
That was the reason why the
United States put North Korea

00:17:10.228 --> 00:17:12.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
on the states
sponsor of terror list,

00:17:12.497 --> 00:17:17.769
and it also shows you just
the brutality and just
the insanity because they

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:23.241 align:start size:91% position:9%
downed a civilian airliner
killing 115 people
on board just to disrupt

00:17:23.341 --> 00:17:26.245 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Olympics
that was going to
be held in South Korea.

00:17:29.047 --> 00:17:32.250
<i> NARRATOR: The DPRK was
 banned from competition.</i>

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:35.587
<i> But the games went on,
 a huge coming out party,</i>

00:17:36.087 --> 00:17:40.558
<i> a turning point for Seoul
 as it pulled further away
 from the north politically,</i>

00:17:40.658 --> 00:17:43.528 align:start size:72% position:28%
<i> economically
 and culturally.</i>

00:17:44.496 --> 00:17:47.866
<i> It only fueled the rivalry
 between the two Koreas.</i>

00:17:50.435 --> 00:17:55.340
<i> Then, on New Years Day 2018,
 Kim Jong-Un gives a speech</i>

00:17:55.441 --> 00:17:58.677 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> as tensions on
 the Korean peninsula
 reach a searing point.</i>

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:33.010 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
HILL: At first, I think
there was a considerable or a
preponderance of views to the

00:18:33.111 --> 00:18:36.381 line:0%
effect that this is
all an effort to create
wedges between the

00:18:36.481 --> 00:18:38.583
United States and South Korea.

00:18:38.683 --> 00:18:41.786
It's also an effort really,
to show South Korea that

00:18:41.886 --> 00:18:45.190 align:start size:88% position:13%
North Korea can be a good
neighbor even if it has
nuclear weapons.

00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:50.863
<i> NARRATOR: This "olive branch"
 was heard around the world.</i>

00:18:51.563 --> 00:18:53.131
-The IOC has approved...

00:18:53.231 --> 00:18:56.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Moon Jae-in
 invites the north to
 march together at the games.</i>

00:18:57.369 --> 00:18:59.938 align:start size:91% position:9%
ALBRIGHT: I can
understand what President
Moon is trying to do, now,

00:19:00.038 --> 00:19:04.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of they are living
there in this very dangerous
area, and these issues,

00:19:05.477 --> 00:19:07.846 align:start size:88% position:13%
and they're much more
complicated than just
one issue like missiles.

00:19:07.946 --> 00:19:09.748
It's their way of life.

00:19:15.654 --> 00:19:19.258 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The North Korean
 delegation arrived at the
 Olympic games lead by</i>

00:19:19.358 --> 00:19:23.428 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>Kim's younger sister and
closest confident, Kim Yo-Jong.</i>

00:19:25.163 --> 00:19:29.868 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Her presence captivated
 the South Koreans,
 part curiosity, part relief</i>

00:19:30.468 --> 00:19:33.872
<i> that she appeared so
 poised and confident.</i>

00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:37.909 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
TERRY: North Koreans
won on that whole image
makeover contest.

00:19:38.843 --> 00:19:42.080
Kim Yo-Jong was called Ivanka
of the Kim administration,

00:19:42.547 --> 00:19:44.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
she was hugely popular
in South Korea,

00:19:44.683 --> 00:19:46.451
she seemed human,
she seemed normal,

00:19:46.551 --> 00:19:48.486
she was charming,
she was smiling.

00:19:48.586 --> 00:19:51.889 align:start size:91% position:9%
PENCE: We'll be telling
the truth about
North Korea at every stop.

00:19:52.657 --> 00:19:55.827 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: The
 American delegation, led
 by Vice President Pence</i>

00:19:55.928 --> 00:19:58.563 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> held talks with
 North Korean defectors,</i>

00:19:58.663 --> 00:20:01.600
<i> implored the south to ignore
 overtures from the north,</i>

00:20:02.734 --> 00:20:04.969
<i> met with the family
 of Otto Warmbier,</i>

00:20:05.536 --> 00:20:08.106 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> the University of Virginia
 student who died soon</i>

00:20:08.206 --> 00:20:11.042
<i> after being released from a
 North Korean prison in a coma,</i>

00:20:12.277 --> 00:20:15.881 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> and avoided
 a state dinner so not be
 with the DPRK delegation.</i>

00:20:20.285 --> 00:20:23.221
<i> During the opening ceremonies
 the body language could not</i>

00:20:23.322 --> 00:20:26.892 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> be more evident as
 Pence sat stone faced.</i>

00:20:27.526 --> 00:20:29.894
TERRY: Then when the
joint team walked in.

00:20:29.994 --> 00:20:31.763 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's not only
North Korean Olympians,

00:20:31.863 --> 00:20:34.399 align:start position:0%
there were South Korean
Olympians that were walking in.

00:20:34.499 --> 00:20:37.936 align:start size:91% position:9%
You can stand up,
you can stand up and cheer
because this is your ally,

00:20:38.804 --> 00:20:42.106 align:start size:97% position:3%
South Korea is hosting
the Olympics and you're seeing
the South Korean athletes also

00:20:42.206 --> 00:20:45.444 align:start size:84% position:16%
coming in, with
North Korean athletes,
so you should stand up

00:20:45.944 --> 00:20:47.746
and be welcoming.

00:20:47.846 --> 00:20:51.516 align:start size:91% position:9%
I didn't think we
scored any kind of
points on that image front.

00:20:52.851 --> 00:20:57.055
<i> NARRATOR: It's on this visit
 that Kim Yo-Jong hand delivers
 a letter from her brother,</i>

00:20:57.689 --> 00:21:01.226
<i> inviting President Moon
 to meet him in person.</i>

00:21:01.693 --> 00:21:03.595
<i> Washington watches.</i>

00:21:04.129 --> 00:21:08.400 align:start size:97% position:3%
ALBRIGHT: President Moon
is somebody that is regarded
more as a liberal within their

00:21:09.434 --> 00:21:14.740 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
system, had come forward with
the idea that there needed
to be more cooperation.

00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:21.746 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I also do think
that there are those who

00:21:21.846 --> 00:21:26.350 align:start size:88% position:13%
believe in the
crazy man theory that
some of the threats that

00:21:26.684 --> 00:21:30.122 align:start size:88% position:13%
President Trump made
I think it's conceivable

00:21:30.222 --> 00:21:33.558
had some role in changing the
mind of the North Koreans,

00:21:34.693 --> 00:21:39.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think the question is:
What happens next?

00:21:43.134 --> 00:21:46.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Both Washington and
 Seoul agree to keep up the
 diplomatic momentum</i>

00:21:46.938 --> 00:21:49.074
<i> that began since the new year.</i>

00:21:49.174 --> 00:21:52.911 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> And president Moon
 Jae-in sends a ten-member
 delegation to Pyongyang.</i>

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:59.584
<i> Kim Jong-Un calls the
 four-hour meeting an
 "open hearted talk...</i>

00:21:59.684 --> 00:22:04.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> actively improving the
 north-south relations and
 ensuring peace and stability</i>

00:22:05.323 --> 00:22:07.993
<i> on the Korean peninsula."</i>

00:22:09.761 --> 00:22:13.932
<i> Washington remains skeptical
 saying that the south should
 not normalize relations with</i>

00:22:14.032 --> 00:22:16.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> the north without discussion
 of denuclearization.</i>

00:22:17.936 --> 00:22:22.407
-We remained determined to
achieve a denuclearization of

00:22:22.507 --> 00:22:25.177
the Korean peninsula.

00:22:28.213 --> 00:22:32.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: But President Moon,
 like a matchmaker, persuades
 the north and the US</i>

00:22:32.451 --> 00:22:38.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> to soften their positions,
 insisting that the two
 initiatives move in parallel,</i>

00:22:38.723 --> 00:22:42.827
<i> urging the US to start
 talks with the DPRK.</i>

00:22:43.128 --> 00:22:47.232 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Kim Jong-Un says he will
 put denuclearization of
 the peninsula on the table.</i>

00:22:50.068 --> 00:22:53.405
<i> And three days later
 Moon's diplomats are
 at the White House</i>

00:22:53.505 --> 00:22:56.541 line:0%
<i> carrying a letter
 from chairman Kim.</i>

00:23:09.287 --> 00:23:13.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The first time
 a sitting American president
 will meet face to face with a</i>

00:23:13.191 --> 00:23:15.226
<i> leader of North Korea.</i>

00:23:15.794 --> 00:23:17.762 align:start size:91% position:9%
PRESIDENT TRUMP:
Of the Korean Peninsula...

00:23:17.862 --> 00:23:22.367 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: Many in the
 diplomatic community are
 surprised, and concerned.</i>

00:23:24.135 --> 00:23:28.707 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> An unconventional president
 meeting an unpredictable
 dictator, as equals.</i>

00:23:30.675 --> 00:23:34.979
<i> A president known more
 for behaving on instinct
 than precedent who shuns</i>

00:23:35.079 --> 00:23:39.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> preparation or study, speaking
 directly with a famously
 thinned skinned impulsive</i>

00:23:41.319 --> 00:23:45.924
<i> dictator, all while the
 White House is embroiled
 in multiple scandals,</i>

00:23:47.592 --> 00:23:49.761
<i> a growing global trade war,</i>

00:23:49.861 --> 00:23:52.630
<i> and the US State Department
 and national security team</i>

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:54.899
<i> are in flux.</i>

00:23:55.200 --> 00:23:58.836
<i> Secretary of state
 Rex Tillerson is
 soon fired by Trump.</i>

00:23:59.537 --> 00:24:03.175
<i> National security
 advisor HR McMaster
 resigns afterward.</i>

00:24:04.276 --> 00:24:08.012
ALBRIGHT: The issue is
how prepared President
Trump will be for it.

00:24:08.479 --> 00:24:14.152
Usually, a summit meeting
takes place towards the end
of negotiations where the

00:24:15.954 --> 00:24:19.624
President can then come in
and put the last stone in,

00:24:20.759 --> 00:24:23.495
and really add
some piece to it,

00:24:23.595 --> 00:24:26.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
but not having done the
building of the whole thing.

00:24:26.898 --> 00:24:29.934
And so, it will take
incredible discipline.

00:24:30.969 --> 00:24:34.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
HILL: If it fails, if one
of them walks out on a huff,

00:24:34.305 --> 00:24:36.841
if one of them suggests,
"No. We can't do this,"

00:24:36.941 --> 00:24:38.977
then, where are
you going to go?

00:24:39.077 --> 00:24:42.580
Because you've already put in
your closer and your closer,

00:24:43.481 --> 00:24:48.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
your leader should be able
to kind of nail down the last
two issues that are out there.

00:24:49.520 --> 00:24:53.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
Instead, you have your
leaders starting the process.

00:24:54.092 --> 00:24:56.995 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
RICHARDSON: I think
they're both very much
alike, they're autocratic,

00:24:57.095 --> 00:24:58.463 line:0%
they're unpredictable.

00:24:58.563 --> 00:25:04.302 align:start position:0% line:0%
and, uh, it could come out a
decent outcome but we're unsure.

00:25:05.970 --> 00:25:11.776
And I've said to the Trump
administration, the gamble
of talking to Kim Jong-Un

00:25:11.877 --> 00:25:16.114 align:start size:88% position:13%
is a huge gamble, but
I think it's the right
gamble, but be prepared.

00:25:17.348 --> 00:25:18.883
They're relentless.

00:25:18.983 --> 00:25:23.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we're not prepared, we
don't have our act together,
we put up unrealistic

00:25:23.588 --> 00:25:26.291
expectations, they're
going to outsmart us.

00:25:28.260 --> 00:25:31.096 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: The wheels are
 literally in motion.</i>

00:25:31.363 --> 00:25:34.332 align:start size:88% position:13%
RICHARDSON: I've seen
that train, nobody else
could ride in that train.

00:25:36.001 --> 00:25:39.738 align:start size:81% position:19%
the good news is that
he's starting to talk
to other leaders.

00:25:43.041 --> 00:25:45.810
<i> NARRATOR: It's March 27, 2018.</i>

00:25:45.910 --> 00:25:50.248 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Kim has not traveled
 outside of the DPRK since
 he assumed power in 2011.</i>

00:25:51.249 --> 00:25:54.318 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And he has yet to meet
 with another head of state.</i>

00:25:54.418 --> 00:25:57.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
RICHARDSON: They're going
to China to ask for something
and that's diplomacy,

00:25:59.256 --> 00:26:02.093
you get squeezed,
you do something.

00:26:02.493 --> 00:26:07.899 align:start size:84% position:16%
And this is irrational
actor, Kim Jong-Un,
taking these steps.

00:26:09.500 --> 00:26:15.073
I believe, I'm not sure,
I'm not there but this is
what he's probably doing.

00:26:17.876 --> 00:26:21.846
<i> NARRATOR: One month before
 he meets with Moon, chairman
 Kim in a surprise move,</i>

00:26:21.946 --> 00:26:26.417 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> arrives in Beijing to
 meet president Xi Jinping
 for the first time.</i>

00:26:27.885 --> 00:26:30.988
TERRY: I think he was doing a
couple things, I think he was
trying to get some sort of

00:26:31.089 --> 00:26:34.525 align:start size:88% position:13%
sanctions relieved, some
sort of to see where
China is in all of that.

00:26:35.226 --> 00:26:38.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
Assure China that China's
interests would be protected,
but I think he also took an

00:26:38.963 --> 00:26:41.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
opportunity to sort of
showcase himself as a leader.

00:26:42.433 --> 00:26:47.705
I think he really used it
to normalize his image, as
a normal leader of a normal

00:26:48.272 --> 00:26:52.644
country, a modern leader
of a modern nation, here
he brought his very young,

00:26:52.744 --> 00:26:55.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
attractive wife and other
senior North Korean officials,

00:26:55.780 --> 00:26:58.249 align:start size:78% position:22%
spent four days
with President Xi.

00:26:58.350 --> 00:27:01.953 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's President Xi,
his wife, Kim Jong-Un
and his attractive wife,

00:27:02.053 --> 00:27:04.588
drinking, laughing, talking.

00:27:04.689 --> 00:27:10.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
So a great image makeover
for Kim, and I think it was
very smart to have done that.

00:27:13.264 --> 00:27:16.901
<i> NARRATOR: Japanese
 prime minister Shinzo Abe
 meets with Trump to</i>

00:27:17.001 --> 00:27:19.471 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> assure Japan's
 interests are not in peril.</i>

00:27:21.372 --> 00:27:25.075 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> And President Trump
 confirms that then
 CIA chief, Mike Pompeo,</i>

00:27:26.010 --> 00:27:30.514 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> met secretly
 with Kim Jong-Un two weeks
 earlier, on Easter weekend,</i>

00:27:31.482 --> 00:27:34.252 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> beginning
 the planning process of
 the Trump-Kim summit.</i>

00:27:34.819 --> 00:27:38.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: And he just
left North Korea, had a great
meeting with Kim Jong-Un,

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:44.295 align:start size:91% position:9%
got along with him
really well, really great.

00:27:45.996 --> 00:27:48.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: Pompeo is poised
 to become Secretary of State.</i>

00:27:49.700 --> 00:27:53.203 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And hard liner, former
 UN ambassador John Bolton,</i>

00:27:53.304 --> 00:27:56.041 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> is appointed National
 Security Advisor.</i>

00:28:01.478 --> 00:28:04.616 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> One week before Kim Jong-Un
 and Moon Jae-In meet,</i>

00:28:05.116 --> 00:28:08.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> North Korea declares
 it will halt all nuclear
 and long-range missile tests.</i>

00:28:10.554 --> 00:28:13.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> And as Kim shifts national
 focus to the north's economy,</i>

00:28:14.258 --> 00:28:17.629 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> he says he will shutdown
 one of his nuclear test sites.</i>

00:28:18.429 --> 00:28:20.131
<i> President Trump tweets,</i>

00:28:20.231 --> 00:28:24.335 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> "This is very good news for
 North Korea and the world,
 big progress."</i>

00:28:25.737 --> 00:28:29.373 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> Now on the table is
 the denuclearization of
 the Korean peninsula,</i>

00:28:29.974 --> 00:28:34.945
<i> and discussion of a peace
 treaty, officially ending the
 Korean war which concluded</i>

00:28:35.045 --> 00:28:38.450 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> with only an armistice,
 ceasing seventy
 years of hostility.</i>

00:28:48.126 --> 00:28:53.130 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The Panmunjom truce
 village traverses both North
 and South Korea inside the</i>

00:28:53.230 --> 00:28:56.434 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Demilitarized Zone
 along the 38th parallel.</i>

00:28:57.935 --> 00:29:02.106
<i> Here President Moon
 and chairman Kim meet
 for the first time</i>

00:29:02.206 --> 00:29:05.944
<i> on April 27th, 2018.</i>

00:29:08.012 --> 00:29:11.783 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> Kim becomes the first
 North Korean leader to ever
 to set foot in the south.</i>

00:29:13.851 --> 00:29:17.789 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The optics show
 a warm and congenial
 burgeoning relationship.</i>

00:29:18.322 --> 00:29:21.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
TERRY: Well it was
really interesting to
watch Kim Jong-Un in terms of

00:29:21.325 --> 00:29:23.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
body language, his voice,
how he was handling himself.

00:29:25.129 --> 00:29:30.934
He's nothing like his father,
who actually was a very big
introvert, and was not social.

00:29:31.802 --> 00:29:34.973 align:start size:91% position:9%
He looked like Kim II-Sung
to me, his grandfather.

00:29:35.073 --> 00:29:38.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was warm, he was effusive,
he was touchy-feely.

00:29:38.276 --> 00:29:41.179
He was affectionate, he
laughed whole-heartedly.

00:29:41.279 --> 00:29:44.515 align:start size:91% position:9%
So, he came across as
actually a charming person,

00:29:45.182 --> 00:29:48.453 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
a social person who can
engage with people,
laughing and joking.

00:29:49.053 --> 00:29:52.891 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
So, all of that
was very interesting to
me, as a Korea watcher.

00:29:55.126 --> 00:29:59.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: The day long
 summit ends with a pledge to
 formally end the Korean war</i>

00:29:59.797 --> 00:30:03.201 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> and a declaration
 to denuclearize
 the Korean peninsula.</i>

00:30:04.502 --> 00:30:08.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Another date is set to start
 negotiations in mid-May.</i>

00:30:09.640 --> 00:30:14.045
<i> But fast-moving events in
 the coming months begin to
 raise the stakes of whether</i>

00:30:14.145 --> 00:30:17.182
<i> a summit with Kim and
 Trump will even happen.</i>

00:30:19.183 --> 00:30:23.588
<i> The next day Trump holds
 a campaign-style rally in
 Macomb County, Michigan.</i>

00:30:24.289 --> 00:30:25.723
PRESIDENT TRUMP: So we
are doing very well.

00:30:25.823 --> 00:30:28.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
I spoke to the
president this morning of
South Korea for a long time.

00:30:28.826 --> 00:30:31.362 align:start size:78% position:22%
They just had a
very good meeting.

00:30:31.462 --> 00:30:32.964
He gives us tremendous credit.

00:30:33.064 --> 00:30:35.132
He gives us all the credit.

00:30:35.232 --> 00:30:38.435 align:start size:91% position:9%
I had one of the fake news
groups this morning...

00:30:38.836 --> 00:30:41.539
(crowd boo's).

00:30:45.142 --> 00:30:50.582 align:start size:91% position:9%
They were saying, "What do
you think President Trump
had to do with it?"

00:30:51.282 --> 00:30:54.152 align:start size:91% position:9%
I'll tell you what,
like how about everything?

00:30:59.257 --> 00:31:01.992 align:start position:0%
<i>NARRATOR: Once the South
Koreans thought of Donald Trump</i>

00:31:02.092 --> 00:31:05.363 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> as much of a
 danger as Kim Jong-Un.</i>

00:31:06.964 --> 00:31:11.101
<i> But now for months, they have
 been thanking Trump for making</i>

00:31:11.201 --> 00:31:14.104 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> the start of a
 reconciliation possible,</i>

00:31:14.204 --> 00:31:17.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> some believe it's to
 appeal to his ego and maintain
 the momentum of the talks.</i>

00:31:21.946 --> 00:31:24.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> President Moon tells
 his senior secretaries,</i>

00:31:24.948 --> 00:31:28.086
<i> "President Trump should
 win the Nobel Peace Prize.</i>

00:31:28.353 --> 00:31:31.422
<i> What we need is only peace."</i>

00:31:31.956 --> 00:31:35.292 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
ALBRIGHT: There are a
lot of leaders who I
think are playing Trump in

00:31:35.392 --> 00:31:40.064 line:0%
terms of understanding that
if they flatter him, that
they make an impression.

00:31:42.065 --> 00:31:43.267
PRESIDENT TRUMP: The
Nobel Peace prize?

00:31:43.367 --> 00:31:44.802
-Yes sir.

00:31:44.902 --> 00:31:47.638 align:start size:91% position:9%
-Well I just think
President Moon was very
nice when he suggested it.

00:31:47.738 --> 00:31:49.674
I wanna, I wanna get peace.

00:31:49.774 --> 00:31:51.542 align:start size:78% position:22%
The main thing,
we wanna get peace.

00:31:51.642 --> 00:31:54.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: North Korean
 officials start to take
 offense that the president is</i>

00:31:54.778 --> 00:31:57.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> taking all the credit to help
 bring peace to the region.</i>

00:31:58.482 --> 00:32:02.052 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> They claim the sanctions were
 not responsible for Kim coming
 to the negotiating table.</i>

00:32:03.320 --> 00:32:06.557 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And Washington
 is "ruining the mood"
 leading up to peace talks.</i>

00:32:08.226 --> 00:32:12.563
TERRY: It's not all just
US maximum pressure strategy
that led to this point.

00:32:13.464 --> 00:32:18.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think Kim Jong-Un
himself had a strategy,
he now gets to sit down with

00:32:18.135 --> 00:32:20.872
the President of
the United States
for the first time.

00:32:21.105 --> 00:32:23.841
So, I think this shows
that Kim Jong-Un is a
different kind of leader.

00:32:23.941 --> 00:32:27.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he has shown himself
to be bold and astute
and quite smart, actually.

00:32:27.277 --> 00:32:33.584
<i> NARRATOR: Then John Bolton,
 the new national security
 advisor who favors military</i>

00:32:33.684 --> 00:32:38.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> action and regime change
 with hostile nations appears
 on CBS' Face The Nation.</i>

00:32:39.357 --> 00:32:41.926 align:start size:97% position:3%
BRENNAN: But is it
a requirement that Kim Jong-Un
agree to give away those

00:32:42.026 --> 00:32:44.795
weapons before you give
any kind of concession?

00:32:44.895 --> 00:32:46.063 align:start size:81% position:19%
BOLTON:
I think that's right.

00:32:46.163 --> 00:32:49.333
I think we're looking at the
Libya model of 2003, 2004.

00:32:49.767 --> 00:32:53.638 align:start size:91% position:9%
We're also looking at what
North Korea itself has
committed to previously.

00:32:54.839 --> 00:32:58.743
TERRY: North Koreans love to
use Libya as an example of

00:32:58.843 --> 00:33:01.278
why they must keep
nuclear weapons.

00:33:01.378 --> 00:33:03.748
They repeatedly say, look
what happened to Gaddafi.

00:33:04.382 --> 00:33:08.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
Gaddafi gave up nuclear
weapons, then the West helped
the revolt against Gaddafi,

00:33:09.152 --> 00:33:10.854
and now Gaddafi's dead.

00:33:10.954 --> 00:33:14.458 align:start size:91% position:9%
So, when North Koreans
hear John Bolton say we're
pursuing a Libyan model,

00:33:14.558 --> 00:33:18.195 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think this
is not helpful because
North Koreans are always,

00:33:18.295 --> 00:33:20.565 align:start size:84% position:16%
they are afraid of
becoming another Libya.

00:33:22.300 --> 00:33:24.168
<i> NARRATOR: Secretary
 of State Mike Pompeo</i>

00:33:24.268 --> 00:33:27.338
<i> arrives in Pyongyang a second
 time to discuss the summit.</i>

00:33:29.674 --> 00:33:33.844
<i> This time he returns with
 three Americans that were
 jailed in North Korea for</i>

00:33:33.944 --> 00:33:37.014
<i> crimes against the state.</i>

00:33:37.114 --> 00:33:40.318
<i> It's believed to be a
 goodwill gesture by Kim.</i>

00:33:42.253 --> 00:33:45.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> As the US confers with
 anxious allies in the region,</i>

00:33:45.656 --> 00:33:48.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> Kim too makes another
 surprise trip to Beijing.</i>

00:33:50.861 --> 00:33:54.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
TERRY: There's multiple
overlapping interests and
not all of them are aligned.

00:33:54.932 --> 00:34:00.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very complicated,
I speculate that Kim Jong-Un
was showing Xi Jinping

00:34:00.637 --> 00:34:04.742 align:start size:97% position:3%
what a deal with United States
might look like and what does
China think of it;

00:34:05.376 --> 00:34:08.278
because you really
need Chinas buy in.

00:34:08.846 --> 00:34:12.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
Meanwhile, our ally
Japan is very unhappy
how things are unfolding

00:34:12.649 --> 00:34:14.652
even though they can't
really quite say it.

00:34:14.752 --> 00:34:17.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because they are so
worried that United States
is going to make a deal with

00:34:17.621 --> 00:34:20.892 align:start size:84% position:16%
North Korea that
protects US interests.

00:34:20.992 --> 00:34:23.728
South Korea is trying
to be sort of an honest
broker, intermediary,

00:34:23.828 --> 00:34:26.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
but is sort of worried
that everything
is going to blow up,

00:34:26.264 --> 00:34:29.833 align:start size:97% position:3%
so there's a lot going on with
different countries trying
to seek their own interests.

00:34:31.235 --> 00:34:34.671 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: Meanwhile,
 President Trump fulfills
 a campaign promise and</i>

00:34:34.771 --> 00:34:38.476 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> pulls out of the Iran
 nuclear deal amid protests
 by our European allies.</i>

00:34:40.811 --> 00:34:44.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Many speculate what this
 would signal for the upcoming
 summit with the DPRK.</i>

00:34:46.951 --> 00:34:50.454 line:0%
HILL: It would be an
interesting point of
conversation, frankly,

00:34:50.554 --> 00:34:52.956 line:0%
if Kim Jong-Un said
to President Trump,

00:34:53.057 --> 00:34:55.559 line:0%
"We've looked at the Iran deal,

00:34:55.660 --> 00:34:59.930
and you say it's the worst
deal ever, why do you say it's
the worst deal ever because

00:35:00.030 --> 00:35:04.869
I'm not sure we can reach a
deal that's anywhere as good
as the Iran deal from your

00:35:05.770 --> 00:35:08.071
perspective, Mr. President."

00:35:08.171 --> 00:35:12.142
So, I think the President is
going to have to make some

00:35:12.242 --> 00:35:18.415 align:start size:91% position:9%
attitudinal changes
about the Iran deal in a
way that will help if there

00:35:18.515 --> 00:35:20.451
is a prospect of
a North Korea deal.

00:35:22.452 --> 00:35:25.789 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: Wrinkles
 begin to appear as
 the DPRK starts reading</i>

00:35:25.889 --> 00:35:28.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> into statements
 coming out of Washington.</i>

00:35:29.493 --> 00:35:34.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
RICHARDSON: Diplomacy is not
<i> Twitter</i> or<i> Facebook</i> or press
releases or cable news.

00:35:35.699 --> 00:35:39.503 line:0%
Diplomacy is human beings
talking to each other and
reaching an agreement,

00:35:40.404 --> 00:35:45.143
showing respect, showing
respect for culture, letting
the other side save face,

00:35:46.877 --> 00:35:50.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
letting the other side
save credit, building
relationships.

00:35:52.483 --> 00:35:54.719
That's diplomacy.

00:35:56.487 --> 00:36:00.257
<i> NARRATOR: The north releases
 a statement rejecting
 Bolton's Libya model claim.</i>

00:36:01.225 --> 00:36:05.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Referring to him
 as "repugnant," they say they
 will never completely disarm.</i>

00:36:08.666 --> 00:36:12.836
<i> That combined with a joint
 South Korean and American
 military exercise along the</i>

00:36:12.936 --> 00:36:18.543
<i> border of the north is enough
 for the north to cancel the
 next inter-Korean talks and</i>

00:36:19.843 --> 00:36:21.946
<i> puts the Trump-Kim
 summit at risk.</i>

00:36:27.018 --> 00:36:30.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: To save his summit
 with Kim, President Trump
 begins to back pedal on</i>

00:36:31.055 --> 00:36:32.756 line:0%
<i> Bolton's statement.</i>

00:36:32.857 --> 00:36:35.860 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: "Well,
the Libyan model isn't a model
that we have at all when we're

00:36:35.960 --> 00:36:37.461
thinking of North Korea.

00:36:37.561 --> 00:36:41.732
But if we make a deal, I
think Kim Jong-Un is going
to be very, very happy.

00:36:43.267 --> 00:36:45.335
I really believe he's
going to be very happy.

00:36:45.435 --> 00:36:47.170
But this is just the opposite.

00:36:47.271 --> 00:36:52.443
And I think when John Bolton
made that statement, he was
talking about if we're going

00:36:52.543 --> 00:36:57.682
to be having a problem,
because we cannot let
that country have nukes,

00:36:58.849 --> 00:36:59.917
we just can't do it.

00:37:01.284 --> 00:37:03.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: With three
 weeks to the historic summit,</i>

00:37:03.987 --> 00:37:08.992 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> set for June 12th
 2018 in Singapore, the
 tension once again rises.</i>

00:37:10.727 --> 00:37:14.632 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> And President Moon makes
 a trip to Washington in the
 hope he can save the talks.</i>

00:37:16.166 --> 00:37:18.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> To North Korean experts
 this is no surprise.</i>

00:37:19.470 --> 00:37:24.341
<i> The idea of Kim giving up his
 nuclear arsenal wholesale in
 exchange for economic relief,</i>

00:37:25.175 --> 00:37:30.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> was always a non-starter,
 they want their
 own security assured.</i>

00:37:32.383 --> 00:37:36.053 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
HILL: They'll look
for some sort of security
agreement quite possibly,

00:37:36.153 --> 00:37:39.523 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
asking us not to
have any more exercises
with the South Koreans.

00:37:40.457 --> 00:37:44.428 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
Potentially, they
could ask us to remove
troops or potentially,

00:37:44.528 --> 00:37:47.565 align:start size:91% position:9%
they could ask us to
reduce our nuclear arsenal.

00:37:48.966 --> 00:37:52.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> NARRATOR: After meeting
 with Moon, Trump says he can
 live with a slower path to</i>

00:37:52.502 --> 00:37:56.907
<i> denuclearization, reversing
 his earlier demand
 for immediate disarmament.</i>

00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:02.480
<i> It is now that events
 begin at a frantic pace.</i>

00:38:03.514 --> 00:38:08.518 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> The South Korean leadership
 predicts a 99.9% chance
 of the summit continuing.</i>

00:38:09.486 --> 00:38:12.323 line:0%
<i> But the north picks up
 on statements made by
 vice president Pence.</i>

00:38:13.991 --> 00:38:16.994 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
PENCE: You know
there was some talk about
the Libya Model last week,

00:38:17.094 --> 00:38:21.932 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
and as the President
made clear,

00:38:22.566 --> 00:38:26.937 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
this will only end
like the Libya Model ended

00:38:27.037 --> 00:38:28.906 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
if Kim Jong-Un
doesn't make a deal.

00:38:29.006 --> 00:38:30.774 line:0%
-Some people saw
that as a threat.

00:38:30.874 --> 00:38:34.210 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
PENCE: Well I
think it's more of a fact.

00:38:34.778 --> 00:38:36.814 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The North Koreans
 had only harsh words,</i>

00:38:36.914 --> 00:38:39.649 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> calling the vice president
 a "political dummy."</i>

00:38:40.650 --> 00:38:45.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> and continued, "Whether the
 US will meet us at a meeting
 room or encounter us at</i>

00:38:45.222 --> 00:38:50.594 align:start position:0%
<i>nuclear-to-nuclear showdown
is entirely dependent
upon the decision... of the US"</i>

00:38:52.329 --> 00:38:57.735 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
GAUSE: The nuclear
program is intimately tied
into two primary objectives

00:38:59.337 --> 00:39:02.106 line:0%
for Kim Jong-Un and the
North Korean regime.

00:39:02.439 --> 00:39:06.510 align:start size:97% position:3%
One is the survival
of the regime, and two is the
perpetuation of the Kim family

00:39:06.610 --> 00:39:10.081
rule, and the nuclear program
is intimately tied into that.

00:39:12.216 --> 00:39:16.520 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: The next morning,
 Trump blindsides the two
 Koreas and abruptly cancels</i>

00:39:16.620 --> 00:39:21.525 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> the summit expressing
 "tremendous anger and open
 hostility" on North Korea's</i>

00:39:21.625 --> 00:39:25.463
<i> part, but he leaves the
 door open to future talks.</i>

00:39:27.731 --> 00:39:31.435 align:start size:91% position:9%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: I believe
that this is a tremendous
setback for North Korea

00:39:32.202 --> 00:39:34.839 align:start size:84% position:16%
and indeed a
setback for the world.

00:39:36.774 --> 00:39:39.910 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: Two
 days later, chairman
 Kim and President Moon</i>

00:39:40.010 --> 00:39:42.579
<i> meet at the truce village.</i>

00:39:42.846 --> 00:39:45.649 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> They agree to hold
 frequent discussions.</i>

00:39:47.284 --> 00:39:51.822
<i> As the clock ticks, American
 and North Korean officials
 hold back channel meetings.</i>

00:39:53.523 --> 00:39:56.727 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The north openly states
 they are willing to
 continue with the summit.</i>

00:39:58.928 --> 00:40:02.866 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> President Trump thanks
 chairman Kim for a solid
 response to his letter and</i>

00:40:02.966 --> 00:40:06.003
<i> says the White House
 is preparing for
 talks on June 12th.</i>

00:40:08.372 --> 00:40:10.073
<i> President Trump tweets,</i>

00:40:10.173 --> 00:40:13.878 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> "We have put a great
 team together for our
 talks with North Korea.</i>

00:40:13.978 --> 00:40:17.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Meetings are
 currently taking place
 concerning summit and more."</i>

00:40:18.348 --> 00:40:23.587 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
ALBRIGHT: There is no
way to describe to anybody
how long it takes to have

00:40:23.687 --> 00:40:27.191 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
these kind of talks,
and how much preparation
has to come from it.

00:40:28.659 --> 00:40:33.230
Also, what the relationship
is with the allied countries.

00:40:35.999 --> 00:40:39.002 align:start size:84% position:16%
<i> NARRATOR: Now, an event
 that would normally
 take months or years</i>

00:40:39.102 --> 00:40:41.605 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> to arrange is
 happening in days.</i>

00:40:43.173 --> 00:40:47.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Mike Pompeo meets in
 New York City to discuss the
 path to denuclearization with</i>

00:40:47.511 --> 00:40:50.413
<i> Vice Chairman Kim Yong-Choi,</i>

00:40:50.513 --> 00:40:53.717 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> the DPRKs top
 nuclear negotiator.</i>

00:40:54.184 --> 00:40:57.554 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> And in Pyongyang Kim meets
 with Russia's foreign minister</i>

00:40:57.654 --> 00:40:59.890
<i> with an invitation
 to come to Moscow.</i>

00:40:59.990 --> 00:41:02.793 align:start size:81% position:19%
<i> Raising concerns
 with the White House.</i>

00:41:04.294 --> 00:41:05.862
<i> President Trump tweets,</i>

00:41:05.962 --> 00:41:09.433 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> "Our United States team
 has arrived in North Korea
 to make arrangements</i>

00:41:09.533 --> 00:41:13.103 align:start position:0%
<i>for the summit
between Kim Jong Un and myself.</i>

00:41:13.203 --> 00:41:16.973
<i> I truely believe North Korea
 has brilliant potential."</i>

00:41:17.373 --> 00:41:22.012 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
KRISTOF: It has been
incredibly frustrating, and
North Korea has lied to us.

00:41:22.112 --> 00:41:23.713 line:0%
Has cheated us.

00:41:23.813 --> 00:41:27.451 align:start size:91% position:9% line:0%
We indeed have likewise
not fulfilled some of our
obligations to North Korea.

00:41:30.187 --> 00:41:35.593 align:start size:88% position:13%
But the last best
hope of trying to resolve
some of these issues

00:41:35.693 --> 00:41:38.529
is going to be to
rely on diplomacy.

00:41:39.330 --> 00:41:43.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no other way,
there's no alternative to try
to resolve this crisis except

00:41:43.500 --> 00:41:45.502 align:start size:84% position:16%
to try to
negotiate a better one.

00:41:46.369 --> 00:41:50.374 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: After talks
 with Pompeo, Kim Yong-Choi
 arrives at the White House</i>

00:41:50.474 --> 00:41:53.677
<i> carrying a letter
 from Kim Jong-Un,</i>

00:41:54.010 --> 00:41:57.414 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> the first time
 a North Korean dignitary
 visited there since 2000.</i>

00:41:59.783 --> 00:42:03.420 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> After two hours,
 President Trump and
 Vice Chairman Kim Yong-Choi</i>

00:42:04.154 --> 00:42:06.123
<i> emerge from the White House.</i>

00:42:06.823 --> 00:42:09.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
PRESIDENT TRUMP: You people
are going to have to travel
because you'll be in Singapore

00:42:09.826 --> 00:42:13.931 align:start size:88% position:13%
on June 12th and I think
it will be a process.

00:42:14.464 --> 00:42:18.235
I never said it goes in
one meeting, I think it's
going to be a process.

00:42:18.502 --> 00:42:21.772
But the relationships
are building and that's
a very positive thing.

00:42:24.040 --> 00:42:28.845
<i> NARRATOR: Two weeks later,
 after a bruising G-7 summit,
 Trump is accused of further</i>

00:42:29.212 --> 00:42:32.216
<i> alienating traditional allies.</i>

00:42:32.983 --> 00:42:37.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> He leaves for Singapore
 confident that he can forge a
 new relationship with a</i>

00:42:37.221 --> 00:42:41.625 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> traditional adversary;
 insisting he doesn't
 need a lot of preparation.</i>

00:42:43.994 --> 00:42:47.998 align:start size:91% position:9%
HILL: The whole
concern about the summit
was the idea that they were

00:42:48.098 --> 00:42:50.634
essentially going to do it
with very little preparation.

00:42:51.568 --> 00:42:54.637 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
And the president was
going to trust his instincts.

00:42:54.737 --> 00:42:56.006 line:0%
That's one problem.

00:42:56.106 --> 00:42:58.909 line:0%
The second problem
is that sometimes his
instincts are wrong.

00:42:59.009 --> 00:43:02.779
And so that's where you need
to have a lot of preparation.

00:43:03.580 --> 00:43:07.550
They essentially went in with
very little preparation and
they certainly didn't have an

00:43:07.650 --> 00:43:13.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
agreement on the overall
issue of denuclearization
except that North Korea said

00:43:13.890 --> 00:43:16.193
they're in favor of it.

00:43:17.461 --> 00:43:22.099 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> NARRATOR: In Singapore,
 a media frenzy begins as
 over 2500 reporters gather.</i>

00:43:26.303 --> 00:43:29.907
<i> Chairman Kim arrives aboard
 a Chinese state airliner.</i>

00:43:30.207 --> 00:43:35.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> Some say it's a
 message from Xi Jinping
 that the DPRK is his vassal,</i>

00:43:35.913 --> 00:43:38.248
<i> tread lightly.</i>

00:43:41.518 --> 00:43:45.923 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> The prime minister of
 Singapore meets with Kim,
 and everywhere he travels</i>

00:43:47.424 --> 00:43:49.994
<i> he's treated with
 rock star status.</i>

00:43:51.762 --> 00:43:56.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> An international
 pariah now looked upon as a
 statesman who may bring peace</i>

00:43:56.967 --> 00:43:59.770
<i> to a nervous region.</i>

00:44:01.705 --> 00:44:04.842 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> President Trump
 arrives on Air Force One.</i>

00:44:06.910 --> 00:44:11.081
<i> After a state lunch he remains
 in his hotel for the night.</i>

00:44:12.516 --> 00:44:14.284 align:start size:88% position:13%
POMPEO: The president is
fully prepared for the
meeting tomorrow.

00:44:14.384 --> 00:44:17.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have personally had the
opportunity to make sure that
he has had the chance to hear

00:44:17.854 --> 00:44:21.925 align:start size:91% position:9%
lots of different voices,
all of the intended
opportunities and risks and

00:44:22.025 --> 00:44:25.529
that we have put these two
leaders in the right place.

00:44:27.497 --> 00:44:29.232
<i> NARRATOR: In stark contrast,</i>

00:44:29.332 --> 00:44:33.203 align:start size:97% position:3%
<i> Kim seemingly
 relishes the attention as he
 tours the streets of the city.</i>

00:44:36.840 --> 00:44:38.642
<i> Next morning, June 12th,</i>

00:44:38.742 --> 00:44:42.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
<i> the flag draped stage
 is set for the historic
 handshake as the two leaders</i>

00:44:43.413 --> 00:44:46.350 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> meet at 9:04 am
 for the first time.</i>

00:44:48.551 --> 00:44:52.856 align:start size:91% position:9%
<i> They will speak one on
 one with only interpreters
 in the room for 45 minutes.</i>

00:44:55.158 --> 00:44:57.794
HILL: Probably the thing
I worried about the most
was when he was going in

00:44:57.894 --> 00:45:02.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
one on one because
he's not terribly well rooted
in some of the issues and

00:45:02.933 --> 00:45:05.569 align:start size:91% position:9%
I thought he might get spun
around on that.

00:45:05.669 --> 00:45:08.706 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
And we still don't
know what he agreed to.

00:45:18.848 --> 00:45:21.451 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> NARRATOR: After a
 working lunch, the
 two emerge to address an</i>

00:45:21.551 --> 00:45:23.587
<i> anxious global community.</i>

00:45:50.347 --> 00:45:53.416
NARRATOR: The analysis
is that though the
meeting was historic,

00:45:53.516 --> 00:45:56.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
the details of the
agreement were vague at best.

00:45:57.321 --> 00:46:01.725 align:start size:91% position:9%
Trump spent much time
flattering Kim, elevated
him to status of an equal,

00:46:03.126 --> 00:46:06.629 align:start size:88% position:13%
and in a move that
blindsided South Korea,
Japan, and the Pentagon,

00:46:07.630 --> 00:46:12.302
Trump agreed to halt US
led military exercises on
the peninsula potentially

00:46:12.736 --> 00:46:15.372 align:start size:78% position:22%
weakening any
military response.

00:46:15.805 --> 00:46:20.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
HILL: What was signed
was an Agreed Statement,
but when you read the text of

00:46:21.011 --> 00:46:24.148
the Agreed Statement
there's a lot less there
that meets the eye,

00:46:25.148 --> 00:46:29.085 align:start size:88% position:13%
certainly less than
was agreed back in 2005.

00:46:29.185 --> 00:46:35.158
I think they'll need another
statement or better yet ignore
what was done in Singapore and

00:46:35.258 --> 00:46:38.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
just start building something
as the Secretary of State

00:46:38.695 --> 00:46:42.165 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
begins the very
necessary diplomacy.

00:46:43.200 --> 00:46:46.637 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
<i> NARRATOR: The hard
 work of keeping the
 north engaged begins.</i>

00:46:47.204 --> 00:46:50.908 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
<i> And it could draw out
 well beyond the Trump
 administration date of 2020.</i>

00:46:53.309 --> 00:46:56.413 line:0%
<i> But for now, the threat
 of war has been hushed.</i>

00:46:58.181 --> 00:47:00.516 line:0%
HILL: This problem
is not going to be
solved with just the

00:47:00.616 --> 00:47:02.285 line:0%
US and North Korea.

00:47:02.385 --> 00:47:05.321 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
We need to be talking to the
Chinese, we need to be talking
to the South Koreans and

00:47:05.421 --> 00:47:06.890 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
of course we need
to be talking to
the Japanese as well.

00:47:06.990 --> 00:47:08.692 line:0%
Captioned by Cotter
Captioning Services.

